            <ArticleTitle>Transient ST elevation and left ventricular asynergy associated with normal coronary artery in aneurysmal subarachnoid hemorrhage.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1274-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 62-year-old woman presented with transient ST segment elevation and left ventricular asynergy in an acute phase of subarachnoid hemorrhage (SAH). A coronary arteriogram during ongoing ST elevation showed no fixed stenoses or spasm. These findings refute epicardial coronary vasospasm as a cause of transient ST elevation and left ventricular asynergy in patients with SAH.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
